course: dictionary
lesson: 3610
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, so read the words around it to find the right one. «The three march off in single file.» The words single file tell you the children walk in a line, one behind another, so file means a line here.
explain: The best check is to put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word and see if it still makes sense. «The three march off in a line, one behind another» makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Computers use the word too. «A website is a set of files stored on a server» means files are pieces of information kept on a computer. «Ransomware is criminal software that locks files and demands payment» shows that files can be locked, so people can lose them.
fact: A file is a set of information kept together on a computer, like a picture or a document.
fact: A file can also be a folder or box for keeping papers in order.
fact: A nail file is a metal tool for making things smooth.
fact: To file means to put papers away in order, or to smooth something with a file.
fact: «In single file» means in a line, one behind another.
exercise: «The three march off in single file.» What does single file mean? | Alone on a long, empty road | *In a line, one behind another | Holding hands in a circle | Very fast and very loud
exercise: «Ransomware is criminal software that locks files and demands payment.» What is a file here? | A line of children walking together | A metal tool for making things smooth | A cloud that brings rain | *Information kept on a computer, like a photo or a document
exercise: «The number of files that fit is space divided by file size: 100 MB holds 20 photos of 5 MB each.» How many 5 MB photos fit in 100 MB? | *20 | 500 | 100 | 5
test: «She used a nail file to make her nails smooth.» What is a nail file? | A pair of scissors for cutting paper | A small brush for hair | *A metal tool for making things smooth | A bright red nail colour
test: «Mum will file the bills in the box.» What does file mean here? | Read them out loud | *Put them away in order | Throw them in the bin | Write a letter to the bank
exam: «A website is a set of files stored on a server and sent to your browser.» What does file mean in this sentence? | A loud noise made by a machine | *A set of information kept together on a computer | A metal tool for smoothing nails | A line of people walking one behind another
